{
  "id": "fluency-l2-any-term",
  "lesson": "l2-any-term",
  "title": "Fluency: the rule for any term",
  "n": 20,
  "pass": 0.9,
  "minutes": 10,
  "families": [
    {
      "id": "term-from-list",
      "weight": 2,
      "skill": "find a term of an arithmetic sequence",
      "vars": {
        "a": { "int": [-20, 30], "not": [0] },
        "d": { "int": [-9, 9], "not": [0] },
        "k": { "int": [8, 40] }
      },
      "let": { "t2": "a + d", "t3": "a + 2*d", "km": "k - 1", "u": "a + (k - 1)*d", "over": "a + k*d", "flip": "a - (k - 1)*d" },
      "prompt": "An arithmetic sequence begins ${a}, {t2}, {t3}, \\dots$ What is $u_{{{k}}}$?",
      "widget": { "kind": "numeric", "answer": "{u}", "tol": { "abs": 0 }, "placeholder": "A whole number" },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "k-steps", "value": "{over}", "line": "You added {k} steps of {d}, but $u_{{{k}}}$ is only {km} steps after $u_1$." },
        { "id": "difference-sign", "value": "{flip}", "line": "Check the sign of $d$: it is ${t2} - {a:()} = {d}$." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "The first term is {a} and $d = {t2} - {a:()} = {d}$.",
        "$u_{{{k}}}$ is {km} steps after $u_1$, so $u_{{{k}}} = {a} + {km} \\times {d:()} = {u}$."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "nth-term-formula",
      "weight": 1,
      "skill": "write the rule for the nth term",
      "vars": {
        "a": { "int": [-12, 15], "not": [0] },
        "d": { "int": [-9, 9], "not": [0] }
      },
      "let": { "t2": "a + d", "t3": "a + 2*d", "t4": "a + 3*d", "c": "a - d" },
      "where": ["a != d"],
      "prompt": "Write $u_n$ for the sequence ${a}, {t2}, {t3}, {t4}, \\dots$",
      "widget": { "kind": "expression", "answer": "{poly(n; d, c)}", "keyboard": "algebra" },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "n-steps", "tex": "{poly(n; d, a)}", "line": "You added $n$ steps to the first term. At $n = 1$ that gives {t2}, which is $u_2$." },
        { "id": "first-term-times-n", "tex": "{poly(n; a, d)}", "line": "You multiplied $n$ by the first term. The difference, {d}, multiplies $n$." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "The first term is {a} and $d = {t2} - {a:()} = {d}$.",
        "Term $n$ is $n - 1$ steps after the first: $u_n = {a} + (n - 1) \\times {d:()}$.",
        "Expand and collect: $u_n = {poly(n; d, c)}$."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "difference-from-two-terms",
      "weight": 1,
      "skill": "find the common difference from two terms",
      "vars": {
        "p": { "int": [1, 6] },
        "g": { "int": [2, 7] },
        "d": { "int": [-9, 9], "not": [0] },
        "a": { "int": [-20, 20] }
      },
      "let": { "q": "p + g", "up": "a + (p - 1)*d", "uq": "a + (p + g - 1)*d", "rise": "g*d", "gt": "g + 1", "share": "g*d/(g + 1)" },
      "prompt": "An arithmetic sequence has $u_{{{p}}} = {up}$ and $u_{{{q}}} = {uq}$. What is the common difference $d$?",
      "widget": { "kind": "numeric", "answer": "{d}", "tol": { "abs": 0 }, "placeholder": "A number" },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "whole-rise", "value": "{rise}", "line": "That is the whole change from $u_{{{p}}}$ to $u_{{{q}}}$. Share it over the {g} steps." },
        { "id": "counted-terms", "value": "{share}", "line": "You shared the change over {gt} terms, but there are {g} steps between them." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "From $u_{{{p}}}$ to $u_{{{q}}}$ there are ${q} - {p} = {g}$ steps.",
        "The terms change by ${uq} - {up:()} = {rise}$.",
        "So $d = {rise} \\div {g} = {d}$."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "which-term",
      "weight": 1,
      "skill": "find the position of a term",
      "vars": {
        "a": { "int": [-20, 30], "not": [0] },
        "d": { "int": [-9, 9], "not": [0, 1, -1] },
        "m": { "int": [8, 60] }
      },
      "let": { "t2": "a + d", "t3": "a + 2*d", "u": "a + (m - 1)*d", "diff": "(m - 1)*d", "mm": "m - 1", "mp": "m + 1" },
      "prompt": "Which term of ${a}, {t2}, {t3}, \\dots$ equals {u}?",
      "widget": { "kind": "numeric", "answer": "{m}", "tol": { "abs": 0 }, "placeholder": "A position" },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "steps-not-position", "value": "{mm}", "line": "You gave the number of steps of {d}. The position is one more than the steps." },
        { "id": "one-too-many", "value": "{mp}", "line": "You added one too many. Term $n$ is $n - 1$ steps after the first." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "Here $d = {t2} - {a:()} = {d}$, so $u_n = {a} + (n - 1) \\times {d:()}$.",
        "Set $u_n = {u}$: $(n - 1) \\times {d:()} = {diff}$, so $n - 1 = {mm}$.",
        "So $n = {m}$."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
